{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Section 1  \n* This is point 1. The Guardian has issued corrections to several inaccuracies in recent publications, clarifying that the new pet theft law, which criminalizes the abduction of cats and dogs, is only enforceable in England and Northern Ireland—not across the entire UK as previously implied. Additionally, Eileen Burbidge was incorrectly labeled as the founder of Fertifa; she serves as executive director, while the actual founders are Tony Chen and Nick Kuan. The publication also corrected the misstatement regarding Juliet Stevenson’s collaborator, noting it was director Alex Lawther, not “Lowther,” and affirmed that the family in Bend It Like Beckham is Sikh, not Muslim, underscoring the importance of cultural precision in media representation.\n\n***\n\nSection 2  \n* This is point 2. Further corrections were made regarding historical claims, notably that it was Venetia Stanley’s uncle, the third Baron Stanley, not her father, the fourth Baron, who converted to Islam—an error that misrepresented a key detail in the narrative of her relationship with Prime Minister Herbert Asquith. The Guardian also acknowledged a series of other amended articles, including reports on Pavel Durov’s arrest, royal servants’ exhibitions, the Pope’s comments on England’s cricket strategy, Britain’s potential as a tech powerhouse, the controversial Salvator Mundi painting, and the cultural legacy of Last of the Summer Wine. These corrections reflect the publication’s commitment to factual integrity and accountability to its readers, inviting feedback through designated channels to ensure continued accuracy.\n\nSection 3  \nThe Guardian’s corrections demonstrate a responsible editorial approach, acknowledging mistakes swiftly and transparently. Whether correcting geographical scope, professional titles, religious identities, or historical lineage, each amendment reinforces the need for diligence in journalism. These updates not only repair misrepresentations but also educate the public on nuanced details often overlooked in fast-paced reporting. The invitation for readers to submit corrections further fosters a collaborative relationship between the institution and its audience, reinforcing trust and credibility.\n\nSection 4  \nP.P.S We appreciate the vigilance of our readers who help us uphold accuracy—your feedback is vital to maintaining the integrity of our reporting.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.008141071535646915}, {"token": "*", "logprob": -8.702239938429557e-06}, {"token": " This", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " point", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.07355085015296936}, {"token": " Guardian", "logprob": -0.006743175443261862}, {"token": " has", "logprob": -0.11454898864030838}, {"token": " issued", "logprob": -0.011316046118736267}, {"token": " corrections", "logprob": -0.8085998892784119}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.2174537032842636}, {"token": " several", "logprob": -0.012595626525580883}, {"token": " inaccur", "logprob": -0.18199004232883453}, {"token": "acies", "logprob": -1.2993727978027891e-05}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.41351398825645447}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.03775734454393387}, {"token": " publications", "logprob": -1.0024129152297974}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0076011475175619125}, {"token": " clar", "logprob": -0.6825299859046936}, {"token": "ifying", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.007852754555642605}, {"token":